Q1. What is Lombok?

Interview Ready Answer

Lombok is a Java library that automatically generates boilerplate
code during compilation using annotations.

It reduces the need to manually write getters, setters,
constructors, toString(), equals(), and hashCode() methods.

Key Points

• Java library.
• Reduces boilerplate code.
• Uses annotations.
• Generates code during compilation.
• Improves code readability and productivity.

======================================================================

Q2. Why do we need Lombok?

Interview Ready Answer

Lombok reduces repetitive code, improves readability, and increases
developer productivity by automatically generating commonly used
methods.

Advantages

• Less boilerplate code.
• Cleaner classes.
• Better readability.
• Faster development.
• Easier maintenance.
• Widely used in Spring Boot projects.

