Q3. What is @Getter?

Interview Ready Answer

@Getter is a Lombok annotation that automatically generates Getter
methods for all or selected fields during compilation.

Purpose

• Eliminates manual getter methods.
• Improves code readability.

======================================================================

Q4. What is @Setter?

Interview Ready Answer

@Setter is a Lombok annotation that automatically generates Setter
methods for fields during compilation.

Purpose

• Eliminates manual setter methods.
• Reduces boilerplate code.

======================================================================

Q5. What is @Data?

Interview Ready Answer

@Data is the most commonly used Lombok annotation.

It combines multiple Lombok annotations into a single annotation.

@Data automatically generates:

• @Getter
• @Setter
• toString()
• equals()
• hashCode()
• @RequiredArgsConstructor

Benefits

• Less code.
• Cleaner classes.
• Easier maintenance.

======================================================================

Q6. What is @Builder?

Interview Ready Answer

@Builder is a Lombok annotation that implements the Builder Design
Pattern.

It provides a flexible and readable way to create objects,
especially when a class has many fields.

Advantages

• Readable object creation.
• Handles optional fields easily.
• Improves maintainability.

======================================================================

Q7. What is @Slf4j?

Interview Ready Answer

@Slf4j is a Lombok annotation that automatically creates an SLF4J
Logger object.

It removes the need to manually declare and initialize a Logger.

Purpose

• Automatic Logger creation.
• Reduces logging boilerplate code.

======================================================================

Q8. What is @Value?

Interview Ready Answer

@Value is a Lombok annotation used to create Immutable Classes.

It makes all fields final, generates getters, and does not generate
setters, preventing object modification after creation.

Use Cases

• DTOs
• Configuration Classes
• Constants

======================================================================

Q9. Difference between @Getter, @Setter, @Data, @Builder and @Value.

Interview Ready Answer

@Getter

• Generates Getter methods.

------------------------------------------------------------

@Setter

• Generates Setter methods.

------------------------------------------------------------

@Data

• Generates Getter, Setter, toString(), equals(),
  hashCode(), and RequiredArgsConstructor.

------------------------------------------------------------

@Builder

• Implements Builder Design Pattern.
• Provides readable object creation.

------------------------------------------------------------

@Value

• Creates Immutable Classes.
• Generates Getters only.
• No Setters.

